description:
persona-attestors/src/registry.rs:7-18, the doc comment on `probe_sources`:

    /// Probe order (matches SPEC-HIA.md §Platform Detection):
    /// 1. Tailscale socket
    /// 2. SSH agent (SSH_AUTH_SOCK)
    /// 3. OIDC cached tokens
    /// 4. DID keys (PERSONA_DID_KEYS)
    /// 5. GPG keyring
    /// 6. FIDO2 hardware keys

The body probes eight, in this order: Tailscale (line 23), SSH agent (32), OIDC (40), DID keys (45), GPG (54), FIDO2 (62), GNOME Online Accounts (70), PIV/smartcard (80). The last two are missing from the list, and the in-body step comments run `// 7.` and `// 8.` past the end of what the doc claims.

The doc also asserts the order "matches SPEC-HIA.md §Platform Detection", so a reader checking the implementation against the spec will compare against a six-item list and conclude GOA and PIV are unspecified additions.

Second inaccuracy in the same comment: "Each source is probed with a lightweight availability check before inclusion." OIDC is not — line 40-43 pushes `OidcCachedAttestor` unconditionally, with its own inline comment explaining that it scans lazily instead. The doc contradicts the code eight lines below it.

Fix: add items 7 and 8, and note the OIDC exception in the sentence that currently claims it applies to every source.
